# src/apps/daemon/internal/platform/mobilehost

## Purpose
Shared mobile platform seam: socket protection, process lookup, and protected dialing used by both proxy and mobile runtime owners.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `platform` (rank 1; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (5): `captive_portal.go`, `host.go`, `host_test.go`, `tun2socks_adapter.go`, `tun2socks_test.go`

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `mobilehost`.
- Notable exported surface: `Dial`, `DialContext`, `Dialer`, `FindProcessConnection`, `ProcessFinder`, `ProtectSocket`, `RegisterProcessFinder`, `RegisterSocketProtector`, `SetCaptivePortalCallback`, `SocketProtector` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/platform/system/nat`.
- Direct daemon callers: `internal/adapters/mobilebind`, `internal/platform/system`, `internal/runtime/mobilecore`, `internal/runtime/proxy`.

## Invariants
- Platform socket/process hooks have one owner shared by proxy and mobile runtime.
- Protected dialing propagates caller context rather than creating detached lifetime.
- `platform` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
